%% FINAL v2: importing a catalogue from ANY source. The core only sees the neutral page format.

sequenceDiagram
    actor Op as Operator
    participant Cmd as scripts/import.js
    participant Core as core: importCatalog
    participant Source as CatalogSource
    participant Ext as IMSLP API or git clone
    participant Repo as CatalogRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Op->>Cmd: npm run import -- --source imslp --limit N
    Cmd->>Cmd: create adapters for the chosen source (composition root)
    Cmd->>Core: importCatalog(source, repository, options)
    Core->>Repo: acquire importer lock, start or resume run (per source)

    loop until --limit or no more results
        Core->>Source: fetchPage(start, limit)
        Source->>Ext: read raw records (rate limit and retries in the adapter)
        Ext-->>Source: raw data in the source's own format
        Note over Source: adapter validates, cleans and maps to the neutral model
        Source-->>Core: { works, skipped, fetchedCount, moreAvailable }
        Core->>Repo: savePage(run, pageStart, works, fetchedCount, finish)
        Repo->>DB: ONE transaction: upsert composers and works, add pending score_files with licence evidence, advance checkpoint
    end

    Core-->>Cmd: summary (inserted, updated, unchanged, skipped, files queued)
    Cmd-->>Op: printed summary + exit code
    Note over Source,Ext: ImslpSource always returns files = [] (IMSLP robots.txt forbids bot file downloads)
